<title>FRANCE: De Deitrich Ferroviare wins 1 bln deal - paper.</title>
<headline>De Deitrich Ferroviare wins 1 bln deal - paper.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French newspaper Les Echos said French state railway SNCF and Germany's Deutsche Bahn had awarded a contract worth around one billion francs to De Dietrich Ferroviaire, part of the De Dietrich group, and its German partner LPH, a unit of GEC-Alsthom.</p>
<p>A spokesman for De Dietrich said it had no &quot;official information on the subject&quot;.</p>
<p>Les Echos said the contract involved the manufacture of tracks for delivery in two years. The tracks will be used for regional and rural transport.</p>
<p>The two railways along with France's five regions issued the tender at the start of the year.</p>
<p>La Tribune newspaper also reported the contract but gave no value for it.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
